## Appendix A: Quick Start Checklist

- [ ] Choose model variant (splade-max recommended)
- [ ] Prepare corpus with proper chunking (200 tokens, 50 overlap)
- [ ] Encode all documents with SPLADE (batch_size=16, top_k=300)
- [ ] Build inverted index (custom or Elasticsearch)
- [ ] Encode queries at runtime (top_k=100)
- [ ] Retrieve via inverted index lookup
- [ ] Optional: Re-rank with cross-encoder
- [ ] Feed to LLM with citations
- [ ] Monitor sparsity statistics (terms per query/doc)
- [ ] Tune FLOPS regularization if needed

---

## Appendix B: Common Issues & Solutions

| Issue | Cause | Solution |
|-------|-------|----------|
| **Too many terms per query** | λ_q too low | Increase query FLOPS weight |
| **Poor recall** | λ_d too high / top_k too low | Decrease doc FLOPS, increase top_k |
| **Slow indexing** | Large batch size / no batching | Use batch_size=16-32, parallelize |
| **OOM during encoding** | Long sequences / large batch | Reduce max_length, batch_size |
| **Quality drop after quantization** | Too aggressive quantization | Use 8-bit instead of 4-bit |
| **Expansion adds noise** | Model not fine-tuned for domain | Fine-tune on domain data |

